[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Adapter Pattern for Legacy System Integration"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Integrating modern applications with legacy systems often presents significant architectural challenges due to incompatible interfaces, outdated data formats, and rigid communication protocols. The Adapter Design Pattern provides a clean, maintainable structural solution by wrapping an existing legacy component with a new interface expected by the modern client."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding the Problem Space"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Imagine a modern e-commerce platform that processes payments using a standardized interface. The business acquires a legacy payment system that utilizes a completely different method signature and data structure. Refactoring the legacy codebase is risky and expensive, while rewriting it entirely is unfeasible. This is where the Adapter pattern bridges the gap."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Core Components of the Adapter Pattern"},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Target Interface: The domain-specific interface that the modern client code expects to interact with."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Adaptee: The legacy system or service containing useful functionality but possessing an incompatible interface."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Adapter: The class that implements the Target interface and holds a reference to an instance of the Adaptee, translating calls between the two."},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Implementation Example in TypeScript"},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"interface ModernPaymentProcessor {
    processPayment(amountInUSD: number): void;
}

class LegacyBillingSystem {
    makeOldPayment(funds: number, currencyCode: string): void {
        console.log("Legacy system processed " + funds + " " + currencyCode);
    }
}

class LegacyPaymentAdapter implements ModernPaymentProcessor {
    private legacySystem: LegacyBillingSystem;

    constructor(legacySystem: LegacyBillingSystem) {
        this.legacySystem = legacySystem;
    }

    processPayment(amountInUSD: number): void {
        this.legacySystem.makeOldPayment(amountInUSD, "USD");
    }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Legacy Integration"},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep adapters focused solely on translation and lightweight data transformation, avoiding business logic accumulation."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Utilize dependency injection to pass legacy service instances into the adapter for enhanced testability."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Implement robust error handling inside the adapter to catch legacy exceptions and map them to modern domain exceptions."}]
